WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.870
From Marvel favorites to Netflix thrillers,
there's a lot of movies that audiences and

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.790
critics can't seem to agree on.

00:00:06.891 --> 00:00:10.950
Video game movies don't have a reputation
for being particularly good.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.360
In fact, most of them are downright terrible,
even if they do tend to make a profit.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.700
That's why it wasn't much of a surprise when
"Uncharted" got a poor rating on Rotten Tomatoes

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:24.430
from critics, even though it wasn't as critically
reviled as the likes of "Street Fighter" or

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.220
"Hitman: Agent 47."

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.770
Based on the video game series of the same
name, "Uncharted" follows the adventures of

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:34.910
globe-trotting treasure hunter Nathan Drake
and his rival and mentor, Victor "Sully" Sullivan.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.610
Unlike the video game, in which Drake is a
veteran treasure hunter, the movie introduces

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.640
Drake as a newcomer on his first quest.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:47.829
Capitalizing on Tom Holland's post-"Spider-Man"
star power, "Uncharted" made $147 million

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:51.710
domestically and $401 million worldwide — not
too shabby.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.671
Still, there was a big gap between critic
and audience scores for "Uncharted," with

00:00:55.671 --> 00:00:59.440
only 41% of professional reviews being positive.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:04.410
Many critics lambasted the casting and compared
the movie unfavorably to adventure films of

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.715
decades past.

00:01:05.715 --> 00:01:06.215
"Really?"

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:07.030
"Yeah."

00:01:07.254 --> 00:01:08.162
"Wow.

00:01:08.162 --> 00:01:09.252
That's your expert analysis?"

00:01:09.712 --> 00:01:14.170
On the other hand, about 90% of audiences
found "Uncharted" satisfying thanks to its

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:18.190
solid effects, fun fights, and relative similarity
to the source material.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:22.750
Whichever side you land on, the vast discrepancy
between critics and audiences' opinions on

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:26.216
this video game-based blockbuster is hardly
uncharted.

00:01:26.216 --> 00:01:31.840
A24 has risen to the top tier of film distributors
by bringing filmgoers such flicks as "Moonlight,"

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.970
"Green Room," and "Ex Machina" — all films
that have united both critics and audiences.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:40.260
But not every A24 film can bridge that gap.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:45.340
Released in 2016, "The Monster" is an indie
horror that impressed quite a few critics,

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.320
but scared away general audiences.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:51.610
The plot follows an alcoholic mom and her
estranged daughter as they drive through the

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.540
woods on one dark and fateful night.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.990
That's when they get into a wreck in the middle
of nowhere and find themselves confronted

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:59.770
by a man-eating creature.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:03.460
Mother and daughter are forced to spend some
serious family bonding time together as they

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.939
try to survive the night.

00:02:04.939 --> 00:02:08.769
Critics were impressed with the horror flick
from director Bryan Bertino, giving the movie

00:02:08.769 --> 00:02:12.159
an impressive approval rating of 80% on Rotten
Tomatoes.

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:16.510
Praise was heaped upon the film's moody atmosphere,
stripped-down plot, and ability to balance

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.049
big emotions with big scares.

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:22.400
Moviegoers weren't so pleased, though, and
the film wound up with an audience score about

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.400
half as positive.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.269
A lot of horror fans found the movie boring,
simplistic, and predictable, and some were

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:33.859
critical of the film's heavy use of flashbacks
— so they saddled it with a 40% positive rating.

00:02:33.859 --> 00:02:38.499
However, many assert that Zoe Kazan and Ella
Ballentine were impressive as the bickering

00:02:38.499 --> 00:02:39.680
mother and daughter.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.900
It's likely their performances that kept the
divide between the audience and critics from

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.680
growing any more monstrous.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:50.739
From the snobbiest critic to the most casual
moviegoer, everyone loves the Coen Brothers.

00:02:50.739 --> 00:02:55.340
For many of their films — from the gut-churning
"No Country for Old Men" to the uproariously

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:59.159
funny "Raising Arizona" — the gap between
audience score and critic score is practically

00:02:59.159 --> 00:03:00.430
non-existent.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:04.901
Even on the super rare occasions when the
Coens flop, like with "The Ladykillers," audiences

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:06.559
and critics share the hate.

00:03:06.559 --> 00:03:10.530
Of course, there are a few exceptions here
and there, like "Intolerable Cruelty" and

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:15.719
"The Hudsucker Proxy," but the most divisive
movie of the Coens' career is almost definitely

00:03:15.719 --> 00:03:16.719
"Hail, Caesar!"

00:03:16.719 --> 00:03:22.060
Set in 1950s Hollywood, this quirky comedy
follows studio fixer Eddie Mannix as he tries

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:28.109
to calm and corral a group of unhappy actors
and a cadre of communist writers who've kidnapped

00:03:28.109 --> 00:03:29.730
the studio's biggest star.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.629
While critics thought the film was divine,
it seems that audiences wanted to stab "Caesar"

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:34.629
in the back.

00:03:34.629 --> 00:03:39.819
The audience reaction to this quippy period
piece remains a middling 44% on Rotten Tomatoes,

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:43.339
while the critics' approval rating is much
higher, at 86%.

00:03:43.339 --> 00:03:48.169
Most critics adored the loving parody of the
golden age studio system, complete with water

00:03:48.169 --> 00:03:49.989
aerobics and tap dancing.

00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:54.319
However, it seems the humor didn't work for
most moviegoers, and many wished the plot

00:03:54.319 --> 00:03:55.731
wasn't so convoluted.

00:03:55.731 --> 00:03:58.150
"Would that it were so simple."

00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:58.942
"W-would that it t'were so simple."

00:03:58.942 --> 00:04:03.549
Featuring big names like George Clooney, Channing
Tatum, and Scarlett Johansson, you'd think

00:04:03.549 --> 00:04:06.269
everyone would be enamored with "Hail, Caesar!"

00:04:06.269 --> 00:04:08.533
— but in Hollywood, few things are guaranteed.

00:04:08.911 --> 00:04:15.219
Ten years ago, a $200 million "spy vs. spy"
action movie starring two A-list stars would've

00:04:15.219 --> 00:04:17.480
opened on thousands of screens.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.480
These days, movies like that seem to go straight
to streaming.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:24.400
That was the case for "The Gray Man," starring
Ryan Gosling and Chris Evans.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:29.350
Gosling plays the CIA's number one agent,
called Six, who is being hunted down by a

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:32.860
sadistic, mustachioed Lloyd Hansen, played
by Chris Evans.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:37.270
This rollicking ride was directed by the Russo
brothers, who oversaw "Captain America: The

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:40.830
Winter Soldier" and the third and fourth "Avengers"
films.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:44.700
While "The Gray Man" had a limited theatrical
release, its primary venue was people's living

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:49.680
rooms — and critics weren't impressed, nailing
the movie with a rotten rating of 46%.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:50.920
But you know who did like it?

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:54.300
The audience, which gave the movie a score
of 90%.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.520
When it came to the critical response, there
were no shades of gray when it came to "The

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.170
Gray Man" — critic and audience opinions
were clearly black and white.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:06.847
Did anyone really think that "Saw 3D" would
actually be the final chapter of the "Saw" franchise?

00:05:06.847 --> 00:05:12.200
In 2017, fans were tossed back into the world
of deadly puzzles and terrible torture devices

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.730
with "Jigsaw," the eighth installment in the
iconic series.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:19.340
It seems that seven year break in between
films was a pretty good move on the part of

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.430
Twisted Pictures, as the audience approval
rating on Rotten Tomatoes skyrocketed all

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:25.800
the way to the series' highest at 89%.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:31.020
"Saw" fans were glad to have John Kramer back,
appreciated all the new traps, and raved about

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.430
all the film's twists and turns.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:37.640
It goes without saying that critics weren't
too keen on Jigsaw's return — in fact, they

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:40.320
haven't really been nuts about the franchise
as a whole.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.290
While audiences appreciated the plot twists,
critics seemed to find them dull.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:47.860
They also didn't really enjoy the killer's
traps, which they didn't find to be terribly

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.640
unique or groundbreaking.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.306
More than anything, though, most critics were
just bored.

00:05:52.306 --> 00:05:56.171
That's how the film ended up with a measly
critic score of 32%.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:59.645
"You've been weighing in on the wrong side
of the scale."

00:05:59.645 --> 00:06:04.210
"Harry Potter" is the highest-grossing book-to-movie
adaptation of all time, with the film franchise

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:08.530
having grossed nearly $10 billion total in
the worldwide box office.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:12.350
Critics loved the cinematic adventures of
Harry, Hermione , and Ron, with all eight

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:15.240
films in the original series being certified
fresh.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:20.010
The "Fantastic Beasts" prequels set decades
before the Boy Wizard's birth, however?

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:21.180
They didn't fare as well.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:26.530
The second film in the spinoff series – 2018's
"Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald"

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:29.430
– earned rotten reviews from both critics
and fans.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:35.130
It still earned money, though: approximately
$654 million on a $200 million budget, to

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.130
be precise.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:40.540
However, that much fan antipathy is never
a good sign for a franchise moving forward,

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.610
and something was clearly rotten in the Wizarding
World.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:48.840
Warner Brothers still went full speed ahead
with the third film, 2022's "Fantastic Beasts:

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:53.880
The Secrets of Dumbledore," which garnered
lousy reviews and a critics' score of 46%

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.030
on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:07:01.980
It also made much less than its predecessor:
just $405 million worldwide on a $200 million budget.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:05.590
Still, the moviegoers who did see "Dumbledore"
seemed to enjoy it, giving it a much higher

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:08.060
consensus score of 83%.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:12.000
The film is hardly spellbinding, but still
relatively solid, especially coming off the

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.000
universally reviled "The Crimes of Grindelwald."

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:19.420
Directed by Rian Johnson, "Star Wars: The
Last Jedi" follows the continued adventures

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:24.180
of Rey, Finn, and Poe as they try their best
to outrun the First Order, defeat Kylo Ren,

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:27.240
and bring a grizzled Luke Skywalker out of
retirement.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:31.460
Needless to say, the film earned tons of cash,
but despite all that money, this space opera

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:35.270
quickly became one of the most controversial
blockbusters ever made.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:39.910
The fan backlash to "The Last Jedi" was intense
and vitriolic, providing the film with a shockingly

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:43.400
low audience score of 42% on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:47.260
So what caused all the ill will toward Rian
Johnson's sci-fi flick?

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:51.570
Some criticized it for supposedly being too
politically correct, while others simply found

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:52.590
the tone uneven.

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:56.530
However, the biggest complaint was how the
film turned Luke Skywalker into a bitter old

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.810
man who's given up on the Force.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:03.639
While some audiences were appalled with Episode
8, critics went crazy for Johnson's addition

00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:07.990
to the series, giving the movie an extremely
fresh rating of 91%.

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:11.910
Fans may have been upset with Luke, but critics
thought the Jedi's new character arc was a

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:13.260
breath of fresh air.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:17.930
Of course, despite the divided reaction, the
only thing Disney really cared about was the

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:21.436
$1.3 billion the film earned at the box office.

00:08:21.436 --> 00:08:26.851
With more than $27 billion in worldwide grosses
and nearly across-the-board "fresh" critic

00:08:26.851 --> 00:08:31.070
and audience scores on Rotten Tomatoes, the
Marvel Cinematic Universe has enough clout

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.820
to take risks now and then.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.779
Or so Marvel Studios thought.

00:08:34.779 --> 00:08:39.180
One risk they took that didn't pay off was
"Eternals," which boasts the worst critic

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.069
score in the MCU by a significant margin.

00:08:42.069 --> 00:08:46.800
The Chloe Zhao film follows the millennia-long
adventures of the Eternals, god-like beings

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:50.600
who protect the people of Earth from bizarre
creatures called Deviants.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:55.100
The MCU is pretty much critic-proof, but "Eternals"
proved to be the exception when it earned

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:59.400
the MCU's one-and-only cinematic "Rotten"
with a 47%.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:05.000
From critics that is, as moviegoers kinda
liked it, giving "Eternals" a 77% audience score.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.160
That's higher than even "Iron Man 2," "Thor,"
and "Captain America: The First Avenger."

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:13.370
"When you love something, you protect it.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:17.970
It is the most natural thing in the world."

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:23.809
However, the world voted with their wallets,
and "Eternals" earned a meager $164 million

00:09:23.809 --> 00:09:28.550
domestic and $402 million worldwide on a $200
million budget.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:33.519
Surprising no one, when Marvel dropped its
plans for Phases 5 and 6 at San Diego Comic

00:09:33.519 --> 00:09:35.820
Con, "Eternals 2" wasn't on the lineup.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:41.370
Hollywood loves making movies about the Holocaust,
and as a result, audiences have become enraptured

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:44.129
by films like "Schindler's List" and "The
Pianist."

00:09:44.129 --> 00:09:48.199
However, with all that attention on Nazi war
crimes, there are a lot of atrocities that

00:09:48.199 --> 00:09:49.800
don't get the Hollywood spotlight.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:54.130
For example, there aren't many movies about
the Armenian genocide, in which the Ottoman

00:09:54.130 --> 00:10:00.269
Empire murdered 1.5 million Armenians from
1915 to the early 1920s.

00:10:00.269 --> 00:10:04.250
Director Terry George, however, hoped to right
that wrong by bringing some attention to the

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:09.350
much-neglected tragedy in "The Promise," a
2016 film starring Oscar Isaac, Christian

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.060
Bale, and Charlotte Le Bon.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:16.059
While it seems the film's audience score on
Rotten Tomatoes was initially hit by genocide-deniers

00:10:16.059 --> 00:10:20.992
looking to sabotage the film, the approval
rating eventually bounced all the way up to 92%.

00:10:20.992 --> 00:10:26.369
It seems film fans were impressed by the film's
epic scope, and many considered it an important

00:10:26.369 --> 00:10:29.600
movie for shedding light on an oft-forgotten
event.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:33.889
But critics were far less kind, especially
in regards to the love triangle between Isaac,

00:10:33.889 --> 00:10:35.120
Bale, and Le Bon.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:38.651
As a result, the critics' score sits far lower,
at 51%.

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:43.670
After Topher Grace debuted a forgettable Venom
in "Spider-Man 3," fans of the character had

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:47.149
to wait years for somebody to do their beloved
antihero justice.

00:10:47.149 --> 00:10:52.110
It took over a decade for Tom Hardy to come
along in 2018 and finally give the iconic

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:54.779
symbiote his title role in "Venom."

00:10:54.779 --> 00:10:59.509
Around 80% of audiences enjoyed Tom Hardy's
performance, agreed the action sequences were

00:10:59.509 --> 00:11:02.769
awesome, and seemed to appreciate the film's
sense of humor.

00:11:02.769 --> 00:11:06.709
That wasn't the case for the critics, though:
without Spider-Man in sight, they decided

00:11:06.709 --> 00:11:08.430
"Venom" wasn't worth their time.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:12.300
Only 30% of professional reviewers seem to
have enjoyed the adventures of Eddie Brock

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:13.869
and his goopy parasite.

00:11:13.869 --> 00:11:14.869
"Parasite?!"

00:11:14.869 --> 00:11:17.516
"Yeah, it's a term of endearment, that's all."

00:11:17.516 --> 00:11:18.931
"Apologize!"

00:11:18.931 --> 00:11:19.516
"No."

00:11:19.516 --> 00:11:20.516
"Apologize!"

00:11:20.885 --> 00:11:21.885
"Alright, fine!"

00:11:22.208 --> 00:11:26.339
While fans thought the movie was full of laughs,
critics were actually bothered by the movie's

00:11:26.339 --> 00:11:28.170
tone — or lack thereof.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:32.040
One of their biggest critiques was how the
film jumped from comedy to horror to romance,

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.279
without ever really settling on one genre.

00:11:34.279 --> 00:11:38.199
However, the critics and the fans did agree
on one aspect: everybody wished the movie

00:11:38.199 --> 00:11:40.279
could've been a little more R-rated.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:45.009
Shot on a shoestring budget, "Mohawk" is an
indie revenge thriller that follows two Native

00:11:45.009 --> 00:11:49.319
Americans and a British soldier who are forced
to fight for their lives after ticking off

00:11:49.319 --> 00:11:51.490
a band of bloodthirsty settlers.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:55.829
Even though the movie has some awesome kills
and veers into horror territory, it didn't

00:11:55.829 --> 00:11:57.889
exactly impress the average viewer.

00:11:57.889 --> 00:12:03.179
The movie currently sits at a rather sad audience
score of 32% on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:12:03.179 --> 00:12:06.730
So what didn't moviegoers like about this
brutal revenge flick?

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:10.290
Well, some were turned off by the film's low
budget, while others thought the acting was

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.899
shoddy and over-the-top.

00:12:11.899 --> 00:12:14.399
That didn't stop critics from giving it plenty
of praise, though.

00:12:14.399 --> 00:12:18.240
In addition to sticking up for the actors,
critics felt there was a lot going on beneath

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:22.529
the surface of "Mohawk," applauding it for
its brutal look at America's bloody past.

00:12:22.529 --> 00:12:28.283
As a result, "Mohawk" won a very positive
approval rating from critics, ending up at 84% fresh.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:33.339
It might be hard to believe that a $200 million
blockbuster starring Dwayne Johnson, Ryan

00:12:33.339 --> 00:12:37.929
Reynolds, and Gal Gadot would be a made-for-TV
movie — but in the streaming era, things

00:12:37.929 --> 00:12:39.809
are changing rapidly.

00:12:39.809 --> 00:12:44.019
Released in November 2021, "Red Notice" is
a Netflix original in which Johnson plays

00:12:44.019 --> 00:12:49.019
an Interpol agent forced to partner up with
his old adversary, Reynolds' wise-cracking

00:12:49.019 --> 00:12:51.850
art thief, to track down Gadot's notorious
criminal.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:52.899
"We're not partners.

00:12:52.899 --> 00:12:54.880
This is a marriage of convenience."

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:56.980
"I want a divorce and I'm keeping the kids."

00:12:56.980 --> 00:13:01.949
Hilarity and explosions ensue in a movie that
would have likely topped the box office charts

00:13:01.949 --> 00:13:03.430
had it been released theatrically.

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:08.559
Instead, it topped the streaming charts, becoming
one of Netflix's most-watched movies of all

00:13:08.559 --> 00:13:10.029
time... much to critical dismay.

00:13:10.029 --> 00:13:15.270
"Red Notice" earned a downright rotten score
and 36% positive ratings from critics, with

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.670
many being disappointed by the sum of its
parts.

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:19.490
You know who wasn't disappointed, though?

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.720
The millions upon millions of people who streamed
it.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:27.379
Audiences gave "Red Notice" incredible reviews
and a 92% score, applauding its comedy and

00:13:27.379 --> 00:13:28.620
narrative twists.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.170
It's hard to say how much cash "Red Notice"
would've earned if it had been released theatrically,

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:36.300
but based on its strong audience reviews and
stacked star power, it wouldn't have been

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:38.019
wise to bet against it.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:42.779
Based on the mega-popular video game franchise,
"Warcraft" was a major failure at the domestic

00:13:42.779 --> 00:13:47.600
box office, earning $47 million against its
$160 million budget.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:51.839
Luckily for executives, the movie fared much
better overseas, pulling in a worldwide total

00:13:51.839 --> 00:13:53.970
of $439 million.

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:58.369
Evidently, video game fans around the planet
banded together to give "Warcraft" a reasonably

00:13:58.369 --> 00:14:02.350
impressive audience score of 76% on Rotten
Tomatoes.

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:05.800
Fans of the film have admitted that the acting
is subpar, but they were blown away by the

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:09.970
movie's visual effects — especially when
it came to the CGI orcs.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:13.579
Despite all the computer generated magic,
critics weren't buying what director Duncan

00:14:13.579 --> 00:14:19.920
Jones was selling, and gave the movie a staggeringly
awful Rotten Tomatoes score of 29% as a result.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:23.689
As it turns out, critics weren't as willing
to forgive the bad acting as audiences were,

00:14:23.689 --> 00:14:27.279
and they were especially critical of the lack
of well-developed characters.

00:14:27.279 --> 00:14:31.360
Another roadblock was the extensive mythology
of the world of "Warcraft": it might have

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:35.209
been appealing to people who'd been playing
the games for years, but according to critics,

00:14:35.209 --> 00:14:39.249
all that emphasis on lore just wasn't going
to work for anyone who hadn't already put

00:14:39.249 --> 00:14:40.475
their hours in.

00:14:40.475 --> 00:14:45.910
When "Bright" hit Netflix in 2017, the streaming
service had a major hit on its hands.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:50.489
Over 11 million people watched the fantasy-buddy
cop thriller over its debut weekend, and the

00:14:50.489 --> 00:14:54.720
film quickly became one of the most-watched
originals in Netflix history.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:58.279
Starring Will Smith and Joel Edgerton, the
movie follows two police officers — one

00:14:58.279 --> 00:15:02.839
a human and one an orc — as they're drawn
into a mystical plot involving elves, gangs,

00:15:02.839 --> 00:15:04.529
and a powerful magic wand.

00:15:04.529 --> 00:15:09.069
Netflix viewers seemed to adore this weird
mishmash of genres, giving "Bright" a commendable

00:15:09.069 --> 00:15:11.610
audience score of 83%.

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:15.029
According to the audience reviews on Rotten
Tomatoes, people thought the urban fantasy

00:15:15.029 --> 00:15:20.360
world created by director David Ayers and
screenwriter Max Landis was pretty phenomenal.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:24.029
Critics couldn't have disagreed more, though,
as they called the screenplay weak and the

00:15:24.029 --> 00:15:25.589
allegory hamfisted.

00:15:25.589 --> 00:15:29.559
By the time the critical dust had settled,
"Bright" found itself reeling from both scathing

00:15:29.559 --> 00:15:34.079
reviews and a Rotten Tomatoes critic's score
of 27% to match.

00:15:34.079 --> 00:15:38.550
It seems that while audiences were enamored
with this world of fairies and firefights,

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:42.249
critics found the film empty, lazy, and lacking
any sort of magic.

00:15:42.511 --> 00:15:47.929
Despite how well-received Tom Cruise's movies
often are, there's one popular film from early

00:15:47.929 --> 00:15:51.559
on in his career that critics weren't exactly
convinced by.

00:15:51.559 --> 00:15:52.679
"Top Gun?!"

00:15:52.679 --> 00:15:54.159
"Yes, sir."

00:15:54.159 --> 00:16:02.089
"Top Gun" topped the worldwide charts in 1986
and earned $357 million at the box office.

00:16:02.089 --> 00:16:06.910
Thanks to its stellar performance, and decades
of playing on Saturday afternoons on TNT,

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:11.329
Tony Scott's high-flying action flick has
become a generation-defining classic for millions

00:16:11.329 --> 00:16:12.329
of viewers...

00:16:12.329 --> 00:16:13.899
just not for a good number of critics.

00:16:13.899 --> 00:16:18.889
"Top Gun" has a mediocre critics' score of
58% on Rotten Tomatoes, while its audience

00:16:18.889 --> 00:16:21.850
score rests at a much more respectable 83%.

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:24.190
The critical consensus review on the website
says —

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:28.510
"'Top Gun' offers too little for non-adolescent
viewers to chew on when its characters aren't

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:29.510
in the air."

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:32.860
Well, perhaps it was an adolescent audience
who bestowed "Top Gun" with strong reviews,

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:34.879
quite a bit higher than the critics.

00:16:34.879 --> 00:16:39.160
To show that there were no hard feelings — and
prove that time does indeed heal all wounds

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:43.660
— the 36-years-later legacy sequel "Top
Gun: Maverick" earned near-perfect Rotten

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:46.079
Tomatoes reviews from both fans and critics.

